WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.430
An SBA 7(a) loan is a bank loan the

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.170
U.S. Small Business Administration

3
00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.330
partly guarantees.

4
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:12.410
New rules for buying a business took effect October 1, 2026.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.800
The core rule: 10% of the project cost must come in as equity,

6
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.420
money alongside the loan.

7
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.120
That's the equity injection,

8
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.480
and for a first acquisition it can't be reduced or eliminated.

9
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.220
At least 5%, half of it, must come from your own resources,

10
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.200
such as cash that isn't borrowed.

11
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.910
The other 5% can be a seller note,

12
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.650
but only on full standby for the life of the loan.

13
00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.770
That means the seller gets no payments

14
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.810
on it until the bank loan is repaid.

15
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.420
A bigger seller note, not on full standby,

16
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.740
must be covered by cash flow in the DSCR test.

17
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.760
That's the debt service coverage ratio:

18
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.860
cash flow divided by loan payments,

19
00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.020
at least 1.25x.

20
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.220
Investors can fund part of the 10% too, as minority owners.

21
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.660
Until the loan is repaid, they can take only tax distributions.

22
00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.670
An illustrative $2,000,000 purchase.

23
00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:12.950
The bank loan covers 90%: $1,800,000.

24
00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.450
Your own cash is 5%: $100,000.

25
00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.290
A standby seller note is the last 5%: $100,000.

26
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.920
Every lender has its own appetite, so confirm with your lender.

27
00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.660
The new SBA rules for buying a business.
